    "body": "Sorry, just catching up after BlinkOn.\r\n\r\nI think this is implementation specific and probably applies to other procedures, but I wonder what sorts of guarantees we should be making on the implementation side. On the BT spec level this procedure shouldn't fail, but there are many cases where this could fail on the implementation side e.g. DBus message times out, Android is busy, etc. What should we do in these cases, should we just throw an error or retry the operation?",
